# DEC-260, batch 3 of 4: the member-facing English still written inline in Civicsmith's other modules, keyed (Bob through BOB,
# K3366: a module reads its words by key through setup-words' word(key, vars) and holds no English; DEC-258's model).
# This batch's 35 modules: contradiction, case-grammar, content, case-authoring, consequences, observation-log, queue-
# producers, following, retrieval, case-checker, membership, wizard-scripts, store-door, case-import, ai-runs, inquiry, money,
# textchain, ai-accounts, plan-work, provenance-routes, case-carriage, machinery-producers, leg-earning, ai-use, publication,
# link-sweep, answer-envelope, browserrender, corpus-export, case-account, queuestate, csv, setup-fleet, publish-schedule.
# What it keys: refusal translations by their code (refusal.<CODE>; the design's existing words govern where a code is already
# keyed, and a code another batch keyed is read, not minted again); undetermined and absence reasons, notes, statements, queue
# texts and labels members read in answers, as <module>.<field>.<slug>; the prose of the signed case document, the complete
# edition and the case checker's report (case-grammar, case-authoring, case-checker); contradiction's per-key absence
# sentences; retrieval's query-syntax help. Spelling is American, internal codes and design-document references are dropped
# from member text (the contradiction keys K1-K6 read 'this key'), template variables are {name}. What stays unkeyed, each
# with its reason (refusal details, markdown headings and session-log lines of the documents' own grammar, store-door's
# dispatch notes, retrieval's matching lexicon, the case-file specification, query and header values, diagnostics), is listed
# in words-reads-mod-3.json beside each module's reads.
# Run: python3 words-mod-3.src.py, then node build_words.mjs.
